.SH NAME
shortcuts \- content with shortcuts active
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
shortcuts(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, shortcuts: Shortcuts<M>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBcontent\fR with \fBshortcuts\fR active.
.PP
The widget that listens for keyboard shortcuts.
.PP
\fBshortcuts\fR wraps any content and, while it is in the view, publishes the message bound to a key press (\fBShortcuts\fR). It needs no subscription and no \fBupdate\fR arm in the app: the message just arrives. A focused widget has precedence: when a text input (or an open popover) handled the key, the shortcut does not fire.
